# small_languages

A short essay for the project site arguing the minimalism tenet. Audience:
programmers who have not seen Trellis or Soil before. The C++ figure is
deliberately rough; keep it hedged as "roughly".

```plan
heading 1: Why small languages
paragraph: surface area is what a checker must distrust
sentence: every construct a language adds is another form its checker must distrust
example: C++ has ~20 forms of initialization
contrast: Soil has one
bridge to: what minimalism buys a language written by machines
paragraph:
define: hallucination — an agent emitting plausible code nobody asked for
sentence: an agent hallucinates in proportion to the choices its language offers
restate: fewer forms, fewer places to be wrong
```
